FREE TOKEN repartitions VRAM between KV pages and expert slots at scheduler safe points without restarting or reloading the host expert pool. Generalize the pattern carefully: ResourceWeather changes should alter physical partitioning at explicit safe points, not force whole-system restart and not perturb semantic state.

Find existing Bonfyre safe-point/occurrence boundaries and represent elastic resource leases for hot physical owners:
- memory/cache partitions;
- CPU/GPU/local-model budgets;
- worker concurrency;
- local scratch/body caches;
- provider/session concurrency where the provider exposes mutable quotas.

A safe-point reconfiguration requires:
old resource frame -> barrier/safe point -> new PhysicalExecutionFrame -> continued occurrence lineage.
No in-flight effect may be silently duplicated or lost. External effects require stronger gates than pure derivation.

Proof: shrink then expand one physical budget during a repeated workload; show continuity, no semantic replay, no duplicate external effect, and receipts spanning both frames.
